PxPgPTF_y1jjWzJc-Q0MnZnCgQSnRhh0rTiHIRV2_5oW9zAE168iQ9TkBdecBPHkuUiu0MGgvssVS44TC5D63MlBm5ItF4wiltIHS0ZWTLx1CEMKRGzjQxoFYBhKGWoVHGE7iRaTG6IvVRl5Dc6wH0uArMQmL_q33vfhZqDnxQZMAzxkBzxhnyJAeYm7-D6SLTZc_el5wrfMxRDmjUH9YPN2XxUXhfBr6UFDTWBpARY8VmKB8G25bTTESVV_I-U-rWobwk3st7uWTHacLhs-FW7g1e4XYHbNIfxpqg3PjC3APXAfTlJnZJvwFoi6wuVLowW4A7Fjedlzsgic4rhWee9dIq-A8BlDNkCXrxed9lsJB67x-QK7DcF-HIUUaP66QLY1tukfXNlK8_MX"},{"type":"function_call","id":"fc_0bfe6e1fa8f24ccf016adb3bee413c8191b4f8613118de73d0","call_id":"call_423b6073446749a789cced42a1e7cfab","name":"check_artifact","arguments":"{\"artifact_json\":\"{\\\"base_candidate\\\":9,\\\"patches\\\":[{\\\"op\\\":\\\"add\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/-\\\",\\\"value\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"R002\\\",\\\"inputs\\\":[\\\"H003\\\",\\\"M001\\\"],\\\"output\\\":\\\"N001\\\",\\\"definitions\\\":[\\\"D001\\\"],\\\"rules\\\":[\\\"direct\\\",\\\"forall_introduction\\\"],\\\"locals\\\":[{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"t\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"positive real\\\",\\\"scope\\\":\\\"R002\\\",\\\"start\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"end\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"arbitrary\\\",\\\"declaration\\\":\\\"Fix arbitrary t>0.\\\",\\\"from_inputs\\\":[],\\\"from_local\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[]}],\\\"argument\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Choose a compact time interval J containing t in its interior and compact C supplied by H003. If x is outside C, u is identically q in a spatial neighborhood and throughout J, so all first derivatives vanish there. Smoothness makes e(·,t) continuous and zero off C, hence compactly supported. Euclidean opens are measurable, Lebesgue measure is finite on compact sets, and ℝ is a normed additive group; M001 therefore gives integrability of e(·,t). Since t was arbitrary, the conclusion holds for every positive t.\\\",\\\"uses\\\":[\\\"H003\\\",\\\"M001\\\"],\\\"uses_local\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"u\\\",\\\"e\\\",\\\"t\\\"],\\\"produces\\\":[],\\\"introduces\\\":[],\\\"discharges\\\":[]}],\\\"applications\\\":[{\\\"input\\\":\\\"M001\\\",\\\"at\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"bindings\\\":\\\"X=ℝⁿ, V=ℝ, μ=Lebesgue, f=e(·,t).\\\",\\\"hypothesis_checks\\\":[\\\"ℝⁿ with Borel measurable opens.\\\",\\\"Euclidean opens are measurable.\\\",\\\"ℝ is a normed additive commutative group.\\\",\\\"Lebesgue measure is finite on compact sets.\\\",\\\"Smoothness gives continuity and H003 gives compact support of e(·,t).\\\"]}] }},{\\\"op\\\":\\\"add\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/-\\\",\\\"value\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"R003\\\",\\\"inputs\\\":[\\\"N001\\\",\\\"H003\\\",\\\"M001\\\",\\\"M004\\\",\\\"M005\\\",\\\"M006\\\"],\\\"output\\\":\\\"N002\\\",\\\"definitions\\\":[\\\"D001\\\",\\\"D002\\\"],\\\"rules\\\":[\\\"direct\\\",\\\"forall_introduction\\\"],\\\"locals\\\":[{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"r\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"positive real\\\",\\\"scope\\\":\\\"R003\\\",\\\"start\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"end\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"arbitrary\\\",\\\"declaration\\\":\\\"Fix arbitrary r>0.\\\",\\\"from_inputs\\\":[],\\\"from_local\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[]}],\\\"argument\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Take J=[r/2,3r/2] and C from H003. Then C×J is compact by M005. The smooth scalar field (x,s)↦e_t(x,s) is continuous on C×J, hence bounded there by some finite K. Outside C it vanishes because u=q locally there throughout J. Set b=K·1_C; compact C is measurable of finite Lebesgue measure, so b is integrable. For τ in (r/2,3r/2), F(τ)(x)=e(x,τ) is continuous and measurable, F(r) is integrable by N001, and F′(r)=e_t(·,r) is continuous and strongly measurable. Smoothness gives the pointwise derivative in τ, and |F′(τ)(x)|≤b(x) for every x,τ. M006 applies: its neighborhood, eventual strong measurability, base integrability, derivative measurability, integrable domination and a.e. derivative conditions all hold. It gives differentiability of E at r with E′(r)=∫e_t(x,r)dx. Since r was arbitrary the assertion holds for all r>0.\\\",\\\"uses\\\":[\\\"N001\\\",\\\"H003\\\",\\\"M001\\\",\\\"M004\\\",\\\"M005\\\",\\\"M006\\\"],\\\"uses_local\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"r\\\",\\\"E\\\",\\\"e\\\",\\\"u\\\"],\\\"produces\\\":[],\\\"introduces\\\":[],\\\"discharges\\\":[]}],\\\"applications\\\":[{\\\"input\\\":\\\"M006\\\",\\\"at\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"bindings\\\":\\\"α=ℝⁿ, μ=Lebesgue, 𝕜=E=ℝ, x₀=r, s=(r/2,3r/2), F(τ)(x)=e(x,τ), F′(τ)(x)=e_t(x,τ), bound=K1_C.\\\",\\\"hypothesis_checks\\\":[\\\"r lies in the neighborhood interval.\\\",\\\"F(τ) is continuous and hence strongly measurable for every τ nearby.\\\",\\\"F(r) integrable by N001.\\\",\\\"F′(r) continuous and strongly measurable.\\\",\\\"The continuous e_t is bounded on compact C×J and vanishes off C, giving domination by K1_C.\\\",\\\"K1_C is integrable since C is compact and Lebesgue measure is finite on compact sets.\\\",\\\"Smoothness gives the derivative identity for every x and τ.\\\"]},{\\\"input\\\":\\\"M005\\\",\\\"at\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"bindings\\\":\\\"X=ℝⁿ,Y=ℝ,s=C,t=J.\\\",\\\"hypothesis_checks\\\":[\\\"Euclidean factors are topological spaces.\\\",\\\"C is compact by H003.\\\",\\\"J is compact as a closed bounded interval.\\\"]},{\\\"input\\\":\\\"M004\\\",\\\"at\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"bindings\\\":\\\"α=C×J, β=ℝ, s=C×J, f=e_t.\\\",\\\"hypothesis_checks\\\":[\\\"C×J compact by M005.\\\",\\\"The relevant spaces have their Euclidean uniform structures.\\\",\\\"Smoothness makes e_t continuous.\\\"]}]} }},{\\\"op\\\":\\\"add\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/-\\\",\\\"value\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"R004\\\",\\\"inputs\\\":[\\\"N002\\\",\\\"M001\\\",\\\"M003\\\",\\\"M007\\\"],\\\"output\\\":\\\"N003\\\",\\\"definitions\\\":[\\\"D001\\\",\\\"D002\\\",\\\"D003\\\"],\\\"rules\\\":[\\\"direct\\\",\\\"forall_introduction\\\"],\\\"locals\\\":[{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"r\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"positive real\\\",\\\"scope\\\":\\\"R004\\\",\\\"start\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"end\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"arbitrary\\\",\\\"declaration\\\":\\\"Fix arbitrary r>0.\\\",\\\"from_inputs\\\":[],\\\"from_local\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[]}],\\\"argument\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"At time r, set g_j(x)=u_t·u_{x_j}. These functions and their derivatives are continuous and compactly supported by the support argument from H003, hence integrable by M001. On each x_j-line choose a finite interval containing the support. Apply M007 to g_j and the constant function 1; the endpoint term vanishes, so the integral of ∂_j g_j on each line is zero. Product integrability follows from continuity and compact support; the factor Lebesgue measures are S-finite, so M003 identifies the whole integral with the iterated integral and gives ∫∂_j g_j=0. Expanding ∂_j g_j by the product rule yields ∫u_{x_j}·∂_j u_t=−∫u_t·u_{x_jx_j}. Summing in j and differentiating the exact Frobenius energy density gives ∫e_t=2∫u_t·(u_{tt}−Δ_xu). N002 identifies the left side with E′(r), proving N003.\\\",\\\"uses\\\":[\\\"N002\\\",\\\"M001\\\",\\\"M003\\\",\\\"M007\\\"],\\\"uses_local\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"r\\\",\\\"u\\\",\\\"E\\\",\\\"Δ_x\\\"],\\\"produces\\\":[],\\\"introduces\\\":[],\\\"discharges\\\":[]}],\\\"applications\\\":[{\\\"input\\\":\\\"M007\\\",\\\"at\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"bindings\\\":\\\"A=ℝ,a=−L,b=L,f=g_j,v=1,f′=∂_j g_j,v′=0 on each coordinate line.\\\",\\\"hypothesis_checks\\\":[\\\"ℝ has the required complete normed algebra structures.\\\",\\\"g_j and 1 are continuous on the compact interval.\\\",\\\"Their derivatives exist on its interior.\\\",\\\"The derivatives are continuous and interval-integrable; endpoint values of g_j vanish.\\\"]},{\\\"input\\\":\\\"M003\\\",\\\"at\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"bindings\\\":\\\"α=ℝ^(n−1), β=ℝ, both Lebesgue, real scalar codomain, integrand the coordinate-permuted ∂_j g_j.\\\",\\\"hypothesis_checks\\\":[\\\"Euclidean factors have measurable spaces and Lebesgue measures are S-finite.\\\",\\\"The codomain ℝ is a real normed space.\\\",\\\"The integrand is continuous compactly supported, hence product-integrable by M001.\\\"]}]} }},{\\\"op\\\":\\\"add\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/-\\\",\\\"value\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"R005\\\",\\\"inputs\\\":[\\\"H001\\\",\\\"H002\\\"],\\\"output\\\":\\\"N004\\\",\\\"definitions\\\":[\\\"D003\\\"],\\\"rules\\\":[\\\"direct\\\",\\\"forall_introduction\\\"],\\\"locals\\\":[{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"x\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"ℝⁿ\\\",\\\"scope\\\":\\\"R005\\\",\\\"start\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"end\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"arbitrary\\\",\\\"declaration\\\":\\\"Fix arbitrary x∈ℝⁿ and r>0.\\\",\\\"from_inputs\\\":[],\\\"from_local\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[]},{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"r\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"positive real\\\",\\\"scope\\\":\\\"R005\\\",\\\"start\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"end\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"arbitrary\\\",\\\"declaration\\\":\\\"Fix arbitrary x∈ℝⁿ and r>0.\\\",\\\"from_inputs\\\":[],\\\"from_local\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[]}],\\\"argument\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"S001\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Differentiate H001 in time to obtain 2u·u_t=0, so u·u_t=0. H002 at the same point supplies a real a with u_{tt}−Δ_xu=a u. Taking the dot product with u_t gives u_t·(u_{tt}−Δ_xu)=a(u_t·u)=0. No regularity of a is used.\\\",\\\"uses\\\":[\\\"H001\\\",\\\"H002\\\"],\\\"uses_local\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"u\\\",\\\"Δ_x\\\"],\\\"produces\\\":[],\\\"introduces\\\":[],\\\"discharges\\\":[]}],\\\"applications\\\":[]} }]}\"}","status":"completed"}],"error":null,"incomplete_details":null,"tools":[{"type":"function","name":"search_mathlib","description":"在固定 mathlib 的 Lean 源码中搜索正则表达式，返回至多 100 行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"query":{"type":"string"}},"required":["query"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_mathlib","description":"读取固定 mathlib 中一个 Mathlib/...lean 文件的指定行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start_line":{"type":"integer"},"line_count":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start_line","line_count"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_task_input","description":"Read an explicitly frozen task document by ID; no other local files are accessible.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["id","start","end"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_yui","description":"Read declared Yui rules/templates; no tests, historical runs or personal files.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start","end"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"check_artifact","description":"Check a JSON artifact against the explicit stage contract; this is not automatic mathematical certification.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"submit_artifact","description":"Submit a JSON artifact after its stage checks.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"report_obstacle","description":"Report exact status, location, explanation, basis, partial_progress. SUBSTANTIVE_GAP or SUSPECTED_GAP stops for an actual unsupported mathematical implication; give its premises, conclusion and mathematical grounds. SOURCE_UNAVAILABLE or INPUT_CONFLICT stops for a real source-access/original-input obstacle. Ordinary unfinished drafting, source registration or format work must use TASK_INCOMPLETE: this records progress without ending the stage; continue the actual work. Difficulty or artifact incompletion alone is not a mathematical gap.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"obstacle_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["obstacle_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"probe_library","description":"Query a proved Mathlib theorem and its exact signature/axioms in the offline sandbox. Returns located evidence for an M source; the mathematical statement and applicability still require review.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"declaration":{"type":"string"},"module":{"type":"string"}},"required":["id","declaration","module"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_draft","description":"Read a JSON pointer in your own same-stage candidate after an actual structural check. No other file/stage is accessible; choose a narrow pointer for large objects.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"candidate":{"type":"integer"},"pointer":{"type":"string"}},"required":["candidate","pointer"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false}],"tool_choice":"auto","parallel_tool_calls":false,"prompt_cache_key":"dc41fff5-2330-4070-bb03-c968fb0d644e","prompt_cache_retention":"24h","text":{"format":{"type":"text"},"verbosity":"low"},"top_p":0.98,"top_logprobs":0,"temperature":1.0,"reasoning":{"effort":"high","context":"all_turns","summary":null,"mode":"standard"},"user":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":66860,"input_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2736,"output_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":508},"total_tokens":69596,"attribution":{"items":{"fc_0bfe6e1fa8f24ccf016adb3b0a8810819191ac5c11c35bea1b":{"input_tokens":31,"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"fc_0bfe6e1fa8f24ccf016adb3b0d27a481919451a73dfa444f2a":{"input_tokens":34,"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"fc_0bfe6e1fa8f24ccf016adb3b0fb93c81918735bc34b03fe930":{"input_tokens":34,"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"fc_0bfe6e1fa8f24ccf016adb3b1249f